    text: "Anatolia was rich in copper and silver from the Taurus and Pontic mountains, and Hittite silver served as money across the kingdom. Smiths, potters, carpenters, leatherworkers and weavers worked for the palace and temples and on their own account; the Laws name craftsmen and set fees for their training and work. Iron was worked here earlier than in most places but stayed rare and precious: a Hittite king, writing to an Assyrian ruler who had asked for good iron, replied that it was not the right season for making it, and sent a dagger blade instead. Craft had sacred patrons: the smith god Hasammili and the goddesses of fate who spun and worked each life.",
