    text: "The Hittite Laws include a price list: a sheep for one shekel of silver, a plough ox for twelve, a field or a vineyard by the iku, a garment, wool, oil and wine at set rates, so that barter could be measured against silver. Merchants travelled under the king's protection, and the laws fined anyone who killed one. Goods went by donkey and ox cart over the mountain passes and down to the ports of Ura and Ugarit on the coast. News of the court and of wars came by royal messengers carrying clay tablets in Hittite and in Akkadian, the diplomatic language; letters between Hattusa, Egypt and Babylon reached across the whole Near East.",
