    evidence: "documented",
    title: "Trading on the riverbank",
    text: "Old Kingdom tombs at Saqqara, among them the shared tomb of Niankhkhnum and Khnumhotep, show riverbank markets: women with baskets of fish, vegetables and bread, men offering sandals, cloth and fans, and haggling written in the captions. Sales were reckoned in copper deben and grain but paid in goods. Where boats landed, such exchanges happened daily. In villages like Deir el-Medina, neighbours lent each other donkeys, tools and grain, bought one another's coffins and furniture, sent gifts at festivals and quarrelled when repayment was slow. The ostraca they left show a community where everyone knew what each household had and owed.",
