    text: "Darius's foundation charter from Susa lists where the materials and workers came from: cedar from Lebanon carried by Assyrians and Ionians, gold from Sardis and Bactria, lapis from Sogdiana, stonecutters from Ionia and Sardis, goldsmiths from Media and Egypt, brickmakers from Babylon. At Persepolis the tablets show teams of craftsmen with foremen, and boys learning trades on smaller rations until they drew a man's. In Zoroastrian thought metals were under the protection of Khshathra Vairya, one of the holy immortals, and fire, used by every smith and potter, was sacred and not to be polluted; craft was part of keeping the world in good order, asha, against the Lie.",
