    evidence: "documented",
    title: "Say not 'uff' to them: kindness to parents",
    text: "The Qur'an commands kindness to parents, birr al-walidayn, directly after the worship of God: if one or both reach old age in your care, do not say to them even 'uff', do not rebuke them, but lower to them the wing of humility. Islamic law made the upkeep of needy parents, nafaqa, a legal duty on sons and, where able, daughters, enforceable by the qadi. A hadith places paradise at the feet of mothers. In practice the old lived in the house of a son, the mother often gaining authority over daughters-in-law, and grandparents minded children and kept family memory. Neglect of an old parent brought shame on a household across its whole quarter.",
